feat: port the auth and landing screens to the new design

Auth — rebuilt as their split, not a restyle of the old one
- form column (352px) on the left, editorial column on the right
- serif title, mono field labels, 36px fields with accent focus rings
- live password-strength meter on sign up, keep-me-signed-in on sign in
- "Continue in demo mode" is now a full-width secondary action rather than a
  footnote, with a line explaining what demo mode actually does
- right column carries a serif pull-quote (sign in) or the what-you-get list
  (sign up); it hides under 880px

Landing
- it had its own :root, so the earlier token port never reached it — it was
  still entirely purple. Now on the same OKLCH blue/amber ramp as the app.
- IBM Plex Sans body, Newsreader headline at 62px/-1.8px tracking, mono eyebrow
- headline is their thesis line, left-aligned, 16ch measure
- buttons and nav CTA to their radius and weight
- removed the typewriter (the headline no longer rotates) and its script

Logo is now the ring-with-a-dot mark from the design — it says the product's
name in the shape, which the caret never did.
